      <ul>
      <li>OpenShift Container Platform: With transparent <a href="/openshift-docs-markdown/networking/network_security/configuring-ipsec-ovn#pod-to-pod-ipsec_configuring-ipsec-ovn">pod-to-pod IPsec</a>, the source and destination of the traffic can be identified by the IP address. There is the capability for egress traffic to be <a href="/openshift-docs-markdown/networking/network_security/configuring-ipsec-ovn#nw-ovn-ipsec-north-south-enable_configuring-ipsec-ovn">encrypted using IPsec</a>. By using the <a href="/openshift-docs-markdown/networking/ovn_kubernetes_network_provider/configuring-egress-ips-ovn#configuring-egress-ips-ovn">egress IP</a> feature, the source IP address of the traffic can be used to identify the source of the traffic inside the cluster.</li>
      <li><a href="/openshift-docs-markdown/service_mesh/v2x/ossm-about#ossm-about">Red Hat OpenShift Service Mesh</a>: Provides powerful <a href="/openshift-docs-markdown/service_mesh/v2x/ossm-security#ossm-security-mtls_ossm-security">mTLS capabilities</a> that can transparently augment traffic leaving a pod to provide authentication and encryption.</li>
